speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, there have been discussions among the parties relating to government business for the remainder of this week. I think you will find that there is unanimous consent for the following arrangements. I move the following motion:
That, on Wednesday, November 8, the House, as its first order of business under Government Orders will resume second reading consideration of Bill C-43, an act respecting abortion; that at 6:00 o'clock p.m., this debate will be adjourned to another sitting day so that the House can then move to resume and complete third reading consideration of Bill C-20, An Act to amend the Excise Tax Act and the Excise Act; that any recorded divisions demanded to dispose of the third reading stage of Bill C-20 will be deferred automatically to 12:00 o'clock noon on Thursday, November 9, 1989 and that the hours of sitting for that day shall be extended by the amount of time taken for any such deferred division;
That, on Thursday, November 9, 1989, the hours of sitting and business of the House shall be as set out in the Standing Orders in relation to a Friday sitting day;
That Thursday, November 9, 1989, be designed an allotted day; and
That, when the House adjourns on Thursday, November 9,1989, it shall stand adjourned until 11.00 o'clock a.m., Monday, November 20, 1989.
